{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "06FW", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-points-finite-type}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:acd3d26af747bfb40fa88878d5b7799c4e95ebaec1840b1437272a9064290629", "source_text": "Points of finite type", "source_text_hash": "sha256:506f133bfd08b80aefbb8ae2fb20096b791ae405f332cc0a3a906617fc2a7bec", "unit_id": "tag:06FW:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06FW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(k) \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5541dd7b94e7700cf47a8e14ebc6610e9ee96e9e77eed967450d2807364f1cfe", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dc6425f52ef8d9e67a07fda918ee1a704b7093f04585d6098f74389f11f2a650", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack.\nA finite type point <MATH_0002> is a point which can be represented\nby a morphism <MATH_0003> which is locally of finite type.\nFinite type points are a suitable replacement of closed points for algebraic\nspaces and algebraic stacks. There are always ``enough of them'' for example.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:086a8fa0b9d6614055f69a3b2bdc324b6b2216d24f26bdeec2adbd76699a3cba", "unit_id": "tag:06FW:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06FW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$x \\in |\\mathcal{X}|$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(k) \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$x$", "MATH_0005": "$U$", "MATH_0006": "$u \\in U$", "MATH_0007": "$\\varphi : U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\varphi(u) = x$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-point-finite-type}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e2f192f98b2fc82e29ea161f38bd5ed00af7791f27bc8dc99ac482733b9a3f59", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:edb00e367d8fe138922b98bd53574017cf46173970e5dd19eab705395b759ba2", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an algebraic stack.\nLet <MATH_0002>. The following are equivalent:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> There exists a morphism <MATH_0003>\nwhich is locally of finite type and represents <MATH_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0003> There exists a scheme <MATH_0005>, a closed point <MATH_0006>, and a smooth\nmorphism <MATH_0007> such that <MATH_0008>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:74e5a27c1112425231a45af6a4706766c9180e4d9c1c22783870cbac186253a0", "unit_id": "tag:06FX:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06FW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u \\in U$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(\\kappa(u)) \\to U$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Spec(k) \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$x$", "MATH_0007": "$U \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0008": "$U$", "MATH_0009": "$U \\times_\\mathcal{X} \\Spec(k) \\to U$", "MATH_0010": "$v$", "MATH_0011": "$U \\times_\\mathcal{X} \\Spec(k)$", "MATH_0012": "$u \\in U$", "MATH_0013": "$v$", "MATH_0014": "$U$", "MATH_0015": "$U$", "MATH_0016": "$u$", "MATH_0017": "$U$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-etale-locally-finite-presentation}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-finite-presentation-finite-type}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-composition-finite-type}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-identify-finite-type-points}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-finite-type-points-morphism}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-identify-finite-type-points}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6b2402cf8f794f4c631778fb6ce8e93fa64dc9f524b37ac6cd9b2580e8f813a4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5c4ee543dbdbfc7433566e36e65a9a5a377ff12aa9a1188bd0a6bf874e11cad3", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be as in (2). Then\n<MATH_0003> is of finite type, and <MATH_0004> is\nrepresentable and locally of finite type (by\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>).\nHence we see (1) holds by\nLemma <REF_0003>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nConversely, assume <MATH_0005> is locally of finite type\nand represents <MATH_0006>. Let <MATH_0007> be a surjective smooth morphism\nwhere <MATH_0008> is a scheme. By assumption\n<MATH_0009> is a morphism of algebraic\nspaces which is locally of finite type. Pick a finite type point <MATH_0010> of\n<MATH_0011> (there exists at least one, see\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0004>).\nBy\nMorphisms of Spaces,\nLemma <REF_0005>\nthe image <MATH_0012> of <MATH_0013> is a finite type point of <MATH_0014>.\nHence by\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0006>\nafter shrinking <MATH_0015> we may assume that <MATH_0016> is a closed point of <MATH_0017>, i.e.,\n(2) holds.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:963c770b4621855904fecd5171de316865726415e13e0cad7a1ee17f852939c3", "unit_id": "tag:06FX:proof"}
